{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1759133,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Triathlon","festival_id":516508,"organization_id":509157,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-09-21T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-13T15:50:02+05:30","location":null,"type":"hackathons","public_url":"hackathons\/triathlon-pravrutti-20-ms-ramaiah-university-of-applied-sciences-1759133","region":"online","details":"<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"6\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">About the Event<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Welcome to <strong data-path-to-node=\"6\" data-index-in-node=\"27\">Triathlon<\/strong> &mdash; a three-round technical event run as one connected game. Unlike a normal multi-round event, the rounds are linked: what a team earns in one round becomes a resource it spends in the next, so consistency across all three rounds decides the winner. There is no elimination &mdash; every team plays all three rounds and the scores are added up to find the ultimate champion!<\/p>\n<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"7\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Event Format &amp; Process<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"8\">\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"8,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Team Size:<\/strong> 2&ndash;3 members per team.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"8,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Round 1: Coding &amp; CS Quiz (25 min):<\/strong> A timed quiz on programming and computer science fundamentals, including 'predict the output', 'find the bug', and spotting a hidden mistake in AI-written code. The top 4 teams will play a live buzzer round. <em data-path-to-node=\"8,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"244\">Reward: Your Round 1 score sets your team's budget for Round 2.<\/em><\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"8,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Round 2: PC Build Fix &amp; Adapt (60 min):<\/strong> Teams are given a faulty PC parts list on PCPartPicker and must find and fix the mistakes. Midway through, the requirements change (budget or use-case) and teams must rework the build and briefly justify their choices. <em data-path-to-node=\"8,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"259\">Reward: Your Round 2 score converts into hint points for Round 3.<\/em><\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"8,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Round 3: CTF Puzzle Hunt (50 min):<\/strong> A Jeopardy-style set of cybersecurity puzzles including hidden messages, simple ciphers, web and forensics challenges. One special clue is even hidden on a poster in the CSE block! <em data-path-to-node=\"8,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"216\">Hint points earned in Round 2 can be spent here.<\/em><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"11\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Rules<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"12\">\n<li>Teams must consist of exactly 2 to 3 members.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"12,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">No Elimination:<\/strong> All teams will participate in all three rounds.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"12,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Scoring:<\/strong> The team with the highest combined score across all three rounds wins.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"12,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Tie-Breaker:<\/strong> In the event of a tie, the team that completed Round 3 in the shortest amount of time will be declared the winner.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"12,4,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Anti-Cheat (Round 3):<\/strong> Each team gets team-specific flags so answers cannot be shared. A live scoreboard will be projected during this round.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27034930,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-09-21T02:42:23+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-06T15:50:04+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"online_coding_challenge","combined_